WEBVTT

00:00:22.604 --> 00:00:24.843
Come on, let's say good
night to your brother.

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:33.857
'Night Sam. Good night, love.

00:00:35.469 --> 00:00:36.852
Hey! Dean.

00:00:36.892 --> 00:00:39.196
Daddy! Hey! Buddy.

00:00:39.292 --> 00:00:42.023
What do you think? Sam is ready
to touch around football yet?

00:00:42.023 --> 00:00:43.884
No, daddy. No?

00:00:43.931 --> 00:00:45.611
You got him? I got him.

00:00:48.087 --> 00:00:49.798
Sweet dreams, Sammy.

00:01:21.065 --> 00:01:22.089
John?

00:01:42.943 --> 00:01:45.736
John, is he hungry?

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:48.688
Okay.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.973
Sammy!

00:02:39.469 --> 00:02:40.185
Mary!

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.149
Mary!

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.681
Mary!

00:02:55.389 --> 00:02:56.632
Hey, Sammy.

00:02:58.362 --> 00:02:59.473
Okay?

00:03:16.972 --> 00:03:17.834
Mary!

00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:32.475
Daddy!

00:03:32.568 --> 00:03:34.228
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:03:34.329 --> 00:03:35.639
Don't look back!

00:03:35.825 --> 00:03:37.039
Now, Dean! Go!

00:03:52.695 --> 00:03:53.821
It's okay, Sam.

00:04:05.066 --> 00:04:07.110
I got it. I got it.

00:04:11.059 --> 00:04:11.703
Here.

00:04:27.774 --> 00:04:29.807
Stay back. You have to stay back.

00:04:49.647 --> 00:04:50.076
Sam!

00:04:50.647 --> 00:04:52.341
Get a move on, would ya?

00:04:52.342 --> 00:04:54.442
We were supposed to be
there like 15 minutes ago.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.217
Sam, you coming or what?

00:04:57.808 --> 00:05:01.489
Do I have to? Yes. It'll be fun.

00:05:02.471 --> 00:05:04.213
And where's your costume?

00:05:06.847 --> 00:05:09.211
You know how I feel about Halloween.

00:05:15.654 --> 00:05:18.509
So here's to Sam and his
awesome LSAT* victory.

00:05:18.616 --> 00:05:20.086
All right, all right.
It's not that big a deal.

00:05:20.087 --> 00:05:22.693
Yeah, he acts all humble,
but he scored a 174.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:26.191
Is that good? Scary good.

00:05:26.233 --> 00:05:28.554
See, there you go. You are
a first-Round draft pick.

00:05:29.068 --> 00:05:30.920
You can go to any law school you want.

00:05:30.921 --> 00:05:33.186
Actually, I got an
interview here monday.

00:05:33.654 --> 00:05:36.803
If it goes okay, I think I got
a shot at a full ride next year.

00:05:36.844 --> 00:05:38.729
Hey, it's gonna go great.

00:05:40.138 --> 00:05:40.861
It better.

00:05:40.893 --> 00:05:43.300
How does it feel to be the
golden boy in your family?

00:05:43.306 --> 00:05:44.362
They don't know.

00:05:44.395 --> 00:05:47.187
No? I would be gloating. Why not?

00:05:47.237 --> 00:05:49.257
'Cause we're not exactly the Bradys

00:05:49.309 --> 00:05:51.655
I'm not exactly the
Huxtables. More shots?

00:05:51.687 --> 00:05:53.444
No. No. No. No!

00:05:53.474 --> 00:05:57.515
Seriously, I'm proud of you, and
you're gonna knock them dead on monday.

00:05:57.516 --> 00:05:58.934
You're gonna get that full ride.

00:05:59.297 --> 00:06:00.299
I know it.

00:06:01.134 --> 00:06:02.517
What would I do without you?

00:06:02.625 --> 00:06:04.010
Crash and burn.

00:07:05.848 --> 00:07:07.871
Whoa! Easy, tiger.

00:07:08.491 --> 00:07:09.294
Dean?

00:07:10.916 --> 00:07:12.376
You scared the crap out of me.

00:07:12.376 --> 00:07:13.823
That's cause you're out of practice.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:17.184
Or not.

00:07:17.695 --> 00:07:18.833
Get off of me.

00:07:19.098 --> 00:07:20.863
Dean, what the hell are you doing here?

00:07:20.895 --> 00:07:23.066
I was looking for a beer.

00:07:23.582 --> 00:07:25.415
What the hell are you doing here?

00:07:25.515 --> 00:07:27.216
Ok, all right, we got to talk.

00:07:28.259 --> 00:07:30.768
The phone? If I'd called
would you picked up?

00:07:31.293 --> 00:07:32.128
Sam?

00:07:33.464 --> 00:07:35.526
Jess, hey.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.854
Dean, this is my girlfriend, Jessica.

00:07:39.577 --> 00:07:41.414
Wait. Your brother Dean?

00:07:41.533 --> 00:07:42.702
I love the Smurfs.

00:07:43.271 --> 00:07:47.009
You know, I got to tell you. You are
completely out of my brother's league.

00:07:47.114 --> 00:07:48.565
Just let me put something on.

00:07:48.611 --> 00:07:52.412
No, no. No, I wouldn't
dream of it, seriously.

00:07:53.446 --> 00:07:56.563
Anyway, I got to borrow your boyfriend here,
talk about some private family business, but

00:07:56.564 --> 00:07:57.752
Nice meeting you.

00:07:59.382 --> 00:08:00.358
No.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.387
No, whatever you want to say,
you can say it in front of her.

00:08:04.987 --> 00:08:05.988
Okay.

00:08:07.533 --> 00:08:09.514
Dad hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:10.481 --> 00:08:14.766
So? He's working overtime on a "Miller Time"
shift. He'll stumble back in sooner or later.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.293
Dad's on a hunting trip,

00:08:18.294 --> 00:08:20.710
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:08:25.632 --> 00:08:26.790
Jess, excuse us.

00:08:28.128 --> 00:08:30.391
We have to go outside.

00:08:30.616 --> 00:08:35.294
I mean, come on, you can't just break in the middle
of the night and expect me to hit the road with you.

00:08:35.295 --> 00:08:37.376
You're not hearing me,
Sammy. Dad's missing.

00:08:37.391 --> 00:08:39.196
I need you to help me find him.

00:08:38.984 --> 00:08:42.309
You remember the poltergeist in
Amherst, or the devil's gates in Clifton?

00:08:42.381 --> 00:08:45.715
He was missing then, too. He's
always missing, and he's always fine.

00:08:45.716 --> 00:08:48.072
Not for this long. Now, are
you gonna come with me or not?

00:08:48.389 --> 00:08:49.360
I'm not.

00:08:49.749 --> 00:08:50.464
Why not?

00:08:50.512 --> 00:08:52.810
I swore I was done hunting. For good.

00:08:53.064 --> 00:08:55.816
Come on, it wasn't easy,
but it wasn't that bad. Yeah?

00:08:56.437 --> 00:08:59.625
When I told dad I was scared of the
thing in my closet, he gave me a .45.

00:08:59.657 --> 00:09:00.755
What was he supposed to do?

00:09:00.789 --> 00:09:02.714
I was 9 years old.

00:09:03.441 --> 00:09:05.708
He was supposed to say:
"Don't be afraid of the dark."

00:09:05.766 --> 00:09:07.353
"Don't be afraid of the
dark"? Are you kidding me?

00:09:07.354 --> 00:09:09.506
Of course, you should be afraid.
You know what's out there.

00:09:09.547 --> 00:09:12.198
Yeah I know but still... The way
we grew up after mom was killed

00:09:12.211 --> 00:09:14.756
And dad's obsession to find
the thing that killed her.

00:09:14.801 --> 00:09:17.234
But we still haven't
found the damn thing.

00:09:17.364 --> 00:09:18.906
So we kill everything we can find.

00:09:19.038 --> 00:09:21.336
Save a lot of people doing it, too.

00:09:23.914 --> 00:09:25.664
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:09:27.659 --> 00:09:31.405
The weapon training and
melting the silver into bullets?

00:09:31.482 --> 00:09:34.029
Man, Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:09:34.055 --> 00:09:35.094
So, what are you gonna do?

00:09:35.294 --> 00:09:38.032
Are you just gonna live
some normal, apple-Pie life?

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:38.643
Is that it?

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:41.094
No, not normal. Safe.

00:09:41.621 --> 00:09:43.374
And that's why you ran away.

00:09:46.778 --> 00:09:48.276
I was just going to college.

00:09:48.277 --> 00:09:51.555
It was dad who said if I was
gonna go, I should stay gone.

00:09:53.075 --> 00:09:54.132
And that's what I'm doing.

00:09:54.151 --> 00:09:58.086
Dad's in real trouble right now if
he's not dead already. I can feel it.

00:10:01.107 --> 00:10:02.410
I can't do this alone.

00:10:02.794 --> 00:10:04.026
Yes, you can.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.146
Yeah. Well, I don't want to.

00:10:15.575 --> 00:10:16.975
What was he hunting?

00:10:22.866 --> 00:10:26.065
All right. Let's see. Where
the hell did I put that thing?

00:10:26.131 --> 00:10:28.103
So when dad left, why
didn't you go with him?

00:10:28.335 --> 00:10:31.858
I was working my own gig... This
voodoo thing down in New Orleans.

00:10:32.235 --> 00:10:34.882
Dad let you go on a
hunting trip by yourself?

00:10:35.433 --> 00:10:36.706
I'm 26, dude.

00:10:38.114 --> 00:10:39.839
All right, here we go.

00:10:40.099 --> 00:10:44.368
So dad was checking out this two-Lane
blacktop just outside of Jericho, California.

00:10:44.467 --> 00:10:45.868
About a month ago, this guy...

00:10:46.133 --> 00:10:49.271
They found his car, but he'd
vanished. Completely M.I.A.

00:10:50.099 --> 00:10:51.658
So maybe he was kidnapped.

00:10:51.697 --> 00:10:53.711
Yeah, well, here's another one in April,

00:10:53.854 --> 00:10:59.311
Another one in December '04, '03, '98,
'92... 10 of them over the past 20 years...

00:10:59.606 --> 00:11:02.378
All men, all same
5-Mile stretch of road.

00:11:04.456 --> 00:11:06.539
Started happening more and more, so

00:11:06.572 --> 00:11:08.067
Dad went to go dig around.

00:11:08.089 --> 00:11:09.839
That was about three weeks ago.

00:11:10.243 --> 00:11:12.630
I hadn't heard from him
since, which is bad enough,

00:11:13.867 --> 00:11:15.941
And then I get this
voice mail yesterday.

00:11:16.483 --> 00:11:20.511
<i>Dean, something is starting to
happen. I think it's serious.</i>

00:11:20.599 --> 00:11:22.532
<i>I need to try to figure
out what's going on.</i>

00:11:26.213 --> 00:11:29.468
<i>Be very careful, Dean.
We're all in danger.</i>

00:11:30.135 --> 00:11:31.664
You know there's EVP on that?

00:11:31.762 --> 00:11:34.587
Not bad, Sammy. Kind of
like riding a bike, isn't it?

00:11:35.325 --> 00:11:38.382
All right. I slowed the message
down and ran it through a goldwave,

00:11:38.413 --> 00:11:40.146
Took out the hiss,
and this is what I got.

00:11:41.719 --> 00:11:45.277
<i>I can never go home.</i>

00:11:47.622 --> 00:11:49.215
Never go home.

00:11:54.981 --> 00:11:58.869
You know, in almost two years, I've never
bothered you, never asked you for a thing.

00:12:05.957 --> 00:12:08.533
All right, I'll go.

00:12:09.439 --> 00:12:10.922
I'll help you find him,

00:12:11.145 --> 00:12:13.051
But I have to get back
first thing Monday.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.378
Just wait here.

00:12:14.695 --> 00:12:16.428
What's first thing monday?

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:19.524
I've this...

00:12:21.136 --> 00:12:22.027
I have an interview.

00:12:22.042 --> 00:12:23.848
What? A job interview? Skip it.

00:12:25.651 --> 00:12:29.936
It's a law-School interview, and
it's my whole future on a plate.

00:12:30.008 --> 00:12:30.930
Law school?

00:12:31.808 --> 00:12:33.463
So we got a deal or not?

00:12:37.714 --> 00:12:39.229
Wait, you're taking off?

00:12:39.508 --> 00:12:40.977
Is this about your dad? Is he all right?

00:12:41.117 --> 00:12:43.537
Yeah. You know, just
a little family drama.

00:12:44.009 --> 00:12:46.645
But your brother said he was
on some kind of hunting trip.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.334
Yeah, he's just deer
hunting up at the cabin,

00:12:49.485 --> 00:12:52.726
And he's probably got Jim,
Jack, and Jose along with him.

00:12:52.729 --> 00:12:54.385
We're just gonna go bring him back.

00:12:54.382 --> 00:12:55.474
What about the interview?

00:12:56.264 --> 00:12:57.420
I'll make the interview.

00:12:57.533 --> 00:12:58.960
This is only for a couple days.

00:12:59.066 --> 00:13:01.777
Sam, I mean, please.
Just stop for a second.

00:13:02.717 --> 00:13:03.795
You're sure you're okay?

00:13:04.689 --> 00:13:05.767
I'm fine

00:13:06.551 --> 00:13:09.878
It's just... You want
even talk about your family

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:13.330
And now you're taking off the middle of
the night to spend the week-End with them

00:13:13.548 --> 00:13:16.390
And with Monday coming up...
It's just not kind of your style.

00:13:16.434 --> 00:13:18.741
Hey, everything's gonna be okay.

00:13:19.544 --> 00:13:21.673
I would be back in time, I promise.

00:13:25.382 --> 00:13:26.902
At least tell me where you're going!

00:13:36.953 --> 00:13:38.702
Amy, I can't come over tonight.

00:13:39.672 --> 00:13:42.280
Because I got work in
the morning, that's why.

00:13:43.841 --> 00:13:46.136
Okay, I miss it, my
dad's gonna have my ass.

00:13:51.739 --> 00:13:53.471
Hey, uh, Amy, let me call you back.

00:14:06.785 --> 00:14:08.253
Car trouble or something?

00:14:13.426 --> 00:14:15.456
Take me home.

00:14:16.971 --> 00:14:18.220
Sure, get in.

00:14:34.408 --> 00:14:36.875
So where do you live?

00:14:39.842 --> 00:14:42.403
At the end of Breckenridge Road.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.811
You're coming from a
Halloween party or something?

00:14:50.563 --> 00:14:54.482
You know, um, a girl like you
really shouldn't be alone out here.

00:15:05.769 --> 00:15:07.503
I'm with you.

00:15:18.998 --> 00:15:21.059
Do you think I'm pretty?

00:15:25.852 --> 00:15:27.617
Will you come home with me?

00:15:27.898 --> 00:15:30.676
Um...Hell, yeah.

00:15:50.354 --> 00:15:52.633
Come on. You don't live here.

00:15:54.131 --> 00:15:55.583
I can never go home

00:15:55.942 --> 00:15:59.986
What? What are you talking
about? Nobody lives here.

00:16:00.349 --> 00:16:02.083
Huh, where do you live?

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:10.800
That's good.

00:16:11.659 --> 00:16:13.111
Joke's over, okay?

00:16:16.467 --> 00:16:18.013
You want me to leave?

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:38.752
Hello?

00:16:46.176 --> 00:16:47.643
Hello?

00:17:48.258 --> 00:17:50.459
Hey. You want breakfast?

00:17:50.948 --> 00:17:52.057
No, thanks.

00:17:53.181 --> 00:17:56.928
So how'd you pay for that stuff? You
and dad still running credit-Card scams?

00:17:57.089 --> 00:18:00.368
Yeah, well, hunting ain't
exactly a pro-Ball career.

00:18:01.929 --> 00:18:04.494
Besides, all we do is apply. It's
not our fault they send us the cards.

00:18:04.525 --> 00:18:08.806
Yeah, and what names did you
write on the application this time?

00:18:08.873 --> 00:18:14.513
Uh... Bert Aframian and his son,
Hector. Scored two cards out of the deal.

00:18:14.607 --> 00:18:16.098
Sounds about right.

00:18:16.115 --> 00:18:19.212
I swear, man,you got to update
your cassette-Tape collection.

00:18:19.284 --> 00:18:20.002
Why?

00:18:20.143 --> 00:18:22.102
Well, for one... They're cassette tapes.

00:18:22.103 --> 00:18:23.101
And two...

00:18:23.102 --> 00:18:27.281
Black Sabbath, Motorhead, Metallica?

00:18:27.647 --> 00:18:30.333
It's the greatest hits of mullet rock.

00:18:30.573 --> 00:18:32.862
House rules, Sammy...
driver picks the music,

00:18:33.101 --> 00:18:34.510
Shotgun shuts his cake hole.

00:18:35.276 --> 00:18:37.899
Yo Sammy is a chubby
12-Year-Old. It's...

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:41.678
Sorry, I can't hear you.
The music's too loud.

00:18:58.279 --> 00:18:59.489
Thank you.

00:19:00.697 --> 00:19:03.587
All right. So there's no one matching
dad at the hospital or morgue.

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:04.876
So that's something, I guess.

00:19:08.227 --> 00:19:09.257
Check it out.

00:19:32.909 --> 00:19:33.877
Let's go.

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:39.679
Did you guys find anything?

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:42.380
No! Nothing!

00:19:47.257 --> 00:19:50.448
No sign of struggle, no
footprints, no fingerprints...

00:19:50.449 --> 00:19:51.447
Spotless. It's almost too clean.

00:19:52.321 --> 00:19:53.943
So this kid, Troy...

00:19:53.944 --> 00:19:55.938
He's dating your daughter, isn't he? Ya.

00:19:55.939 --> 00:19:57.020
How's Amy doing?

00:19:57.129 --> 00:19:59.174
She's been putting up
missing posters downtown.

00:20:00.267 --> 00:20:03.000
You had another one like
this last month, didn't you?

00:20:04.186 --> 00:20:05.357
And who are you?

00:20:05.904 --> 00:20:07.340
Federal marshals.

00:20:08.875 --> 00:20:10.999
You two are a little young
for marshals, aren't you?

00:20:11.186 --> 00:20:12.841
Thanks, that's awfully kind of you.

00:20:13.408 --> 00:20:15.329
You did have another one
just like this, correct?

00:20:15.485 --> 00:20:16.234
Yeah, that's right,

00:20:16.484 --> 00:20:18.748
About a mile up the road. There
have been others before that.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:21.502
So this victim... You knew him?

00:20:22.266 --> 00:20:24.249
A town like this,
everybody knows everybody.

00:20:24.312 --> 00:20:27.091
Any connection between the victims
besides that they're all men?

00:20:27.152 --> 00:20:29.057
No. Not so far as we can tell.

00:20:29.416 --> 00:20:30.462
So what's the theory?

00:20:30.591 --> 00:20:31.912
Honestly, we don't know...

00:20:31.913 --> 00:20:34.329
Serial murderer, kidnapping ring.

00:20:34.338 --> 00:20:38.430
Well, that is exactly the kind of crack
police work I'd expect out of you guys.

00:20:38.887 --> 00:20:40.870
Thank you for your time.

00:20:41.338 --> 00:20:43.102
Gentlemen.

00:20:51.576 --> 00:20:52.589
What was that for?

00:20:52.571 --> 00:20:55.211
Why do you have to step on my foot? Why
do you have to talk to police like that?

00:20:55.421 --> 00:20:57.825
Come on. They don't really
know what's going on.

00:20:57.933 --> 00:20:59.090
We're all alone on this.

00:20:59.091 --> 00:21:02.173
If we're gonna find dad, we've got to
get to the bottom of this thing ourselves.

00:21:04.637 --> 00:21:06.230
Can I help you boys?

00:21:06.741 --> 00:21:08.537
No, sir. We were just leaving.

00:21:08.538 --> 00:21:10.829
Agent Mulder, agent Scully.

00:21:19.202 --> 00:21:20.529
I'll bet you that's her.

00:21:20.827 --> 00:21:21.732
Yeah.

00:21:23.699 --> 00:21:25.417
You must be Amy. Yeah.

00:21:25.875 --> 00:21:28.763
Troy told us about you. We're his
uncles. I'm Dean. This is Sammy.

00:21:28.997 --> 00:21:30.356
He never mentioned you to me.

00:21:30.934 --> 00:21:32.151
Well, that's Troy, I guess.

00:21:32.198 --> 00:21:33.898
We're not around much.
We're up in Modesto.

00:21:33.899 --> 00:21:37.801
So we're looking for him, too,
and we're kind of asking around.

00:21:38.005 --> 00:21:40.191
Hey, are you okay? Yeah.

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:42.632
Do you mind if we ask
you a couple questions?

00:21:43.683 --> 00:21:46.364
I was on the phone with
Troy. He was driving home.

00:21:46.365 --> 00:21:51.208
He said he would call me
right back, and he never did.

00:21:51.209 --> 00:21:53.759
He didn't say anything
strange? Or out of the ordinary?

00:21:53.904 --> 00:21:56.746
No, nothing I can remember.

00:21:58.187 --> 00:21:59.530
I like your necklace.

00:22:02.267 --> 00:22:03.500
Troy gave it to me.

00:22:04.146 --> 00:22:08.065
Mostly to scare my parents...
You know, the devil stuff.

00:22:10.536 --> 00:22:12.751
Actually it means just the opposite.

00:22:12.762 --> 00:22:15.493
A pentagram is a
protection against evil.

00:22:15.595 --> 00:22:18.593
Really powerfull, I mean if
you believe in a kind of thing.

00:22:18.738 --> 00:22:21.080
Ok, thank you, Unsolved Mysteries.

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:22.531
Here's the deal, ladies...

00:22:22.532 --> 00:22:26.028
The way Troy disappeared...
Something's not right.

00:22:26.029 --> 00:22:28.128
So if you've heard anything...

00:22:30.416 --> 00:22:31.322
What is it?

00:22:32.009 --> 00:22:32.937
Well, it's just...

00:22:33.020 --> 00:22:35.960
I mean, with all these guys
going missing, people talk.

00:22:36.006 --> 00:22:37.193
What do they talk about?

00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:43.068
It's kind of this local legend.

00:22:43.333 --> 00:22:47.955
This one girl, she got murdered
out on Centennial like decades ago.

00:22:48.558 --> 00:22:51.197
Well, supposedly, she's still out there.

00:22:51.592 --> 00:22:54.975
She hitchhikes, and
whoever picks her up...

00:22:54.976 --> 00:22:58.142
Well, they disappear forever.

00:23:15.208 --> 00:23:17.034
Let me try. I got it.

00:23:18.392 --> 00:23:19.235
Dude.

00:23:20.749 --> 00:23:22.904
You're such a control freak.

00:23:23.638 --> 00:23:26.620
So angry spirits are born out
of violent death, right? Yeah

00:23:26.995 --> 00:23:28.400
Maybe it's not murder.

00:23:36.722 --> 00:23:42.594
This was 1981. Constance Welch, 24 years old,
jumps off Sylvania Bridge, drowns in the river.

00:23:42.625 --> 00:23:44.378
Does it say why she did it? Yeah.

00:23:44.768 --> 00:23:45.330
What?

00:23:46.065 --> 00:23:48.411
An hour before they
found her, she calls 911.

00:23:48.474 --> 00:23:51.619
Her two little kids are in the bathtub.
She leaves them alone for a minute,

00:23:51.620 --> 00:23:52.789
And when she comes back,

00:23:52.861 --> 00:23:54.111
They aren't breathing.

00:23:54.789 --> 00:23:55.804
Both died.

00:23:56.793 --> 00:23:59.375
"Our babies were gone, and
Constance just couldn't bear it,"

00:23:59.376 --> 00:24:00.374
Said husband, Joseph Welch.

00:24:02.747 --> 00:24:04.840
That bridge look familiar to you?

00:24:09.825 --> 00:24:12.823
So this is where Constance
took the swan dive.

00:24:13.119 --> 00:24:14.967
So you think dad would have been here?

00:24:15.747 --> 00:24:18.464
Well, he's chasing the same
story, and we're chasing him.

00:24:19.874 --> 00:24:21.217
Okay, so now what?

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:24.745
Now we keep digging till we
find him. It might take a while.

00:24:24.943 --> 00:24:28.550
Dean, I told you I've got
to get back by... Monday.

00:24:29.689 --> 00:24:31.454
Right. The interview.

00:24:31.501 --> 00:24:33.077
Yeah. Yeah, I forgot.

00:24:33.739 --> 00:24:35.581
You're really serious
about this, aren't you?

00:24:36.580 --> 00:24:38.782
You think you're just
gonna become some lawyer,

00:24:39.157 --> 00:24:40.406
Marry your girl?

00:24:40.469 --> 00:24:41.608
Maybe. Why not?

00:24:41.816 --> 00:24:45.189
Does Jessica know the truth about you?
Does she know about the things you've done?

00:24:45.392 --> 00:24:47.156
No, and she's not ever going to know.

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:49.389
Well, that's healthy.

00:24:49.690 --> 00:24:54.202
You can pretend all you want, Sammy, but sooner or
later you're gonna have to face up to who you really are.

00:24:54.628 --> 00:24:55.386
Who is that?

00:24:55.395 --> 00:24:56.889
One of us. No!

00:24:57.018 --> 00:24:59.553
I'm not like you. This is
not going to be my life.

00:24:59.576 --> 00:25:02.638
Well, you have a responsibility. To dad?

00:25:01.968 --> 00:25:03.669
And his crusade?

00:25:04.043 --> 00:25:07.088
If it weren't for pictures, I
wouldn't even know what mom looks like.

00:25:07.483 --> 00:25:08.857
What difference would it make?

00:25:09.106 --> 00:25:11.246
Even if we do find the
thing that killed her,

00:25:12.042 --> 00:25:14.822
Mom's gone, and she isn't coming back.

00:25:21.052 --> 00:25:23.394
Don't talk about her like that.

00:25:32.572 --> 00:25:33.493
Sam.

00:25:46.294 --> 00:25:48.089
Where'd she go? I don't know.

00:25:52.439 --> 00:25:56.077
What the...? Who's driving your car?

00:26:03.746 --> 00:26:06.587
Come on, Dean. Let's go! Go!

00:26:32.935 --> 00:26:33.794
Dean!

00:26:35.212 --> 00:26:35.883
Dean!

00:26:38.702 --> 00:26:39.545
What?!

00:26:43.304 --> 00:26:45.474
Hey, are you all right?

00:26:46.411 --> 00:26:47.582
I'm super.

00:26:53.279 --> 00:26:54.590
Car all right?

00:26:54.792 --> 00:26:57.384
Yeah, whatever she did to
it, it seems all right now.

00:26:57.619 --> 00:26:59.759
That Constance chick... What a bitch!

00:26:59.992 --> 00:27:02.756
Well, she doesn't want us
digging around, that's for sure.

00:27:04.713 --> 00:27:06.992
So where's the trail
go from here, genius?

00:27:12.473 --> 00:27:14.050
You smell like a toilet.

00:27:17.056 --> 00:27:18.273
One room, please.

00:27:22.130 --> 00:27:24.020
You guys having a reunion or something?

00:27:24.316 --> 00:27:24.988
What do you mean?

00:27:25.320 --> 00:27:29.738
That other guy, Bert Aframian. He came in
and bought out a room for the whole month.

00:28:00.343 --> 00:28:02.899
I don't think he's been here
for a couple days at least.

00:28:05.059 --> 00:28:07.712
Salt, cat's-Eye shells...

00:28:08.135 --> 00:28:11.887
He was worried, trying to
keep something from coming in.

00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:16.009
What do you got here?

00:28:16.476 --> 00:28:19.084
Centennial Highway victims.

00:28:20.629 --> 00:28:21.957
I don't get it.

00:28:22.519 --> 00:28:26.422
I mean, different men,
different jobs, age, ethnicities.

00:28:27.130 --> 00:28:28.895
There's always a connection, right?

00:28:29.722 --> 00:28:31.143
What do these guys have in common?

00:28:46.242 --> 00:28:47.569
Dad figured it out.

00:28:47.838 --> 00:28:49.087
What do you mean?

00:28:49.135 --> 00:28:51.200
He found the same article we did.

00:28:51.201 --> 00:28:54.608
Constance Welch. She's a woman in white.

00:28:57.577 --> 00:28:59.060
You sly dogs.

00:28:59.357 --> 00:29:02.714
All right, so if we're dealing with a woman in white,
dad would have found the corpse and destroyed it.

00:29:02.902 --> 00:29:04.495
She might have another weakness.

00:29:05.018 --> 00:29:07.539
No, dad would want to
make sure. He'd dig her up.

00:29:07.598 --> 00:29:08.960
Does it say where she's buried?

00:29:09.383 --> 00:29:11.178
No, not that I can tell.

00:29:11.694 --> 00:29:13.896
If I were dad, though,
I'd go ask her husband,

00:29:14.317 --> 00:29:15.566
If he's still alive.

00:29:22.122 --> 00:29:25.261
All right, why don't you see if you can
find an address? I'm gonna get cleaned up.

00:29:25.702 --> 00:29:30.589
Hey, Dean, what I said earlier
about mom and dad... I'm sorry.

00:29:31.417 --> 00:29:32.837
No chick-Flick moments.

00:29:34.013 --> 00:29:35.809
All right... jerk.

00:29:36.949 --> 00:29:37.823
Bitch.

00:29:55.110 --> 00:29:58.529
<i>Hey, it's me. It's about 10:20...</i>

00:29:59.044 --> 00:30:03.235
Hey, man. I'm starving. I'm gonna grab a little
something to eat at that diner down the street.

00:30:03.236 --> 00:30:04.541
You want anything?

00:30:04.848 --> 00:30:05.415
No.

00:30:05.415 --> 00:30:06.710
Aframian's buying.

00:30:24.171 --> 00:30:26.701
<i>So come home soon, okay? I love you.</i>

00:30:29.558 --> 00:30:30.089
What?

00:30:30.328 --> 00:30:31.655
Dude, five-O. Take off.

00:30:32.123 --> 00:30:33.138
What about you?

00:30:33.403 --> 00:30:35.995
Uh, they kind of
spotted me. Go find dad.

00:30:37.963 --> 00:30:39.150
Problem, officers?

00:30:39.322 --> 00:30:40.570
Where's your partner?

00:30:40.819 --> 00:30:42.864
Partner? What? What partner?

00:30:50.291 --> 00:30:53.881
So fake U.S. Marshal, fake credit cards.

00:30:54.147 --> 00:30:55.599
You got anything that's real?

00:30:56.146 --> 00:30:57.051
My boobs.

00:30:58.979 --> 00:31:01.118
You have the right to remain silent.

00:31:03.419 --> 00:31:05.605
So you want to give us your real name?

00:31:05.954 --> 00:31:09.202
I told you. It's Nugent, Ted Nugent.

00:31:11.387 --> 00:31:14.385
I'm not sure you realize just
how much trouble you're in here.

00:31:14.386 --> 00:31:18.731
We're talking, like, misdemeanor kind of
trouble or "squeal like a pig" trouble?

00:31:19.090 --> 00:31:21.838
You got the faces of 10 missing
persons taped to your wall,

00:31:22.250 --> 00:31:25.154
Along with a whole lot
of satanic mumbo jumbo.

00:31:25.528 --> 00:31:27.464
Boy, you are officially a suspect.

00:31:27.626 --> 00:31:31.592
That makes sense 'cause when the
first one went missing in '82, I was 3.

00:31:32.138 --> 00:31:35.042
I know you got partners.
One of them's an older guy.

00:31:35.823 --> 00:31:37.790
Maybe he started the whole thing.

00:31:39.466 --> 00:31:41.668
So tell me, Dean...

00:31:44.062 --> 00:31:44.983
Is this his?

00:31:52.545 --> 00:31:54.044
I thought that might be your name.

00:31:55.668 --> 00:31:57.210
See, I leafed through this,

00:31:57.224 --> 00:32:00.794
What little I could make out. I
mean, it's nine kinds of crazy,

00:32:02.391 --> 00:32:04.109
But I found this, too.

00:32:05.182 --> 00:32:10.866
Now, you're staying right here till you
tell me exactly what the hell that means.

00:32:23.134 --> 00:32:26.257
Hi, uh, are you Joseph Welch? Yeah.

00:32:27.141 --> 00:32:28.879
Yeah, he was older, but that's him.

00:32:28.961 --> 00:32:32.321
He came by three or four days
ago, said he was a reporter.

00:32:32.679 --> 00:32:35.146
That's right. We're
working on a story together.

00:32:36.393 --> 00:32:40.406
Well, I don't know what the hell kind of story
you're working on... the questions he asked me.

00:32:40.484 --> 00:32:42.310
About your late wife, Constance.

00:32:43.278 --> 00:32:45.012
He asked me where she was buried.

00:32:45.860 --> 00:32:47.468
And where is that again?

00:32:48.077 --> 00:32:49.591
What? I got to go through these twice?

00:32:49.888 --> 00:32:52.228
It's fact checking, if you don't mind.

00:32:54.851 --> 00:32:58.255
In a plot behind my old
place over on Breckenridge.

00:32:58.869 --> 00:33:00.415
Why did you move?

00:33:01.835 --> 00:33:05.270
I'm not gonna live in the
house where my children died.

00:33:07.981 --> 00:33:10.057
Mr. Welch, did you ever marry again?

00:33:10.182 --> 00:33:13.789
No way. Constance... She
was the love of my life,

00:33:15.380 --> 00:33:17.207
Prettiest woman I ever known.

00:33:17.426 --> 00:33:18.862
So you had a happy marriage?

00:33:22.372 --> 00:33:23.168
Definitely.

00:33:26.244 --> 00:33:28.961
Well, that should do
it. Thanks for your time.

00:33:39.525 --> 00:33:42.358
Mr. Welch, you ever
hear of a woman in white?

00:33:42.539 --> 00:33:43.273
A what?

00:33:43.741 --> 00:33:46.880
A woman in white or
sometimes a weeping woman.

00:33:47.915 --> 00:33:48.899
It's a ghost story.

00:33:49.121 --> 00:33:52.417
Well, it's more of a phenomenon, really.

00:33:52.718 --> 00:33:56.185
They're spirits. They've been
sighted for hundreds of years,

00:33:56.544 --> 00:34:00.750
Dozens of places in Hawaii and
Mexico, lately in Arizona, Indiana.

00:34:00.791 --> 00:34:02.665
All these are different
women, you understand,

00:34:02.950 --> 00:34:04.824
But all share the same story.

00:34:05.761 --> 00:34:08.919
Boy, I don't care much for nonsense.

00:34:09.076 --> 00:34:10.434
You see, when they were alive,

00:34:10.877 --> 00:34:12.907
Their husbands were unfaithful to them,

00:34:13.812 --> 00:34:14.890
And these women,

00:34:15.249 --> 00:34:18.309
Basically suffering from temporary
insanity, murdered their children.

00:34:19.975 --> 00:34:23.317
Then, once they realized what they
had done, they took their own lives.

00:34:23.613 --> 00:34:25.362
So now their spirits are cursed,

00:34:25.690 --> 00:34:27.704
Walking back roads, waterways,

00:34:28.037 --> 00:34:31.097
And if they find an
unfaithful man, they kill him,

00:34:31.534 --> 00:34:33.268
And that man is never seen again.

00:34:34.907 --> 00:34:36.374
You think...

00:34:37.529 --> 00:34:41.215
You think that has something
to do with Constance,

00:34:41.840 --> 00:34:43.010
You smart ass?

00:34:43.603 --> 00:34:44.743
You tell me.

00:34:48.161 --> 00:34:52.626
I mean, maybe... Maybe
I made some mistakes,

00:34:53.204 --> 00:34:54.874
But no matter what I did,

00:34:55.562 --> 00:34:58.295
Constance never would have
killed her own children.

00:34:59.720 --> 00:35:01.812
Now, you get the hell out of here,

00:35:02.250 --> 00:35:03.857
And you don't come back.

00:35:19.303 --> 00:35:21.270
I don't know how many
times I got to tell you.

00:35:21.489 --> 00:35:23.098
It's my high-School locker combo.

00:35:23.524 --> 00:35:25.211
Are we gonna do this all night long?

00:35:25.288 --> 00:35:28.364
We just got a 911. Shots
fired over at Whiteford Road.

00:35:30.316 --> 00:35:31.830
Do you have to go to the bathroom?

00:35:32.460 --> 00:35:33.101
No.

00:35:33.428 --> 00:35:34.490
Good.

00:36:24.381 --> 00:36:27.567
Fake 911 phone call, Sammy?
That's pretty illegal.

00:36:27.847 --> 00:36:28.613
You're welcome.

00:36:28.706 --> 00:36:29.987
Listen, we got to talk

00:36:30.080 --> 00:36:32.817
Tell me about it. So the
husband was unfaithful.

00:36:32.911 --> 00:36:34.597
We are dealing with a woman in white.

00:36:34.674 --> 00:36:37.242
She's buried behind her old house.

00:36:37.263 --> 00:36:38.461
Sammy, would you shut up for a second?

00:36:38.505 --> 00:36:40.628
I can't figure out why he
hasn't destroyed the corpse yet.

00:36:40.831 --> 00:36:43.267
That's what I'm trying
to tell you. He's gone.

00:36:43.662 --> 00:36:44.739
Dad left Jericho.

00:36:44.786 --> 00:36:46.628
What? How do you know?

00:36:47.441 --> 00:36:48.252
I've got his journal.

00:36:48.440 --> 00:36:50.048
He doesn't go anywhere
without that thing.

00:36:50.240 --> 00:36:51.333
Well, he did this time.

00:36:51.396 --> 00:36:52.145
What's it say?

00:36:52.176 --> 00:36:55.268
Same old ex-Marine crap when he
wants to let us know where he's going.

00:36:55.331 --> 00:36:56.137
Coordinates.

00:36:56.140 --> 00:36:57.138
Where to?

00:36:57.138 --> 00:36:58.303
I'm not sure yet.

00:36:58.328 --> 00:37:02.418
I don't understand. I mean,
what can be so important

00:37:02.419 --> 00:37:03.417
That he just gets out
in the middle of the job?

00:37:03.034 --> 00:37:04.797
Dean, what the hell is going on?

00:37:08.262 --> 00:37:09.651
Sam, Sam!

00:37:16.047 --> 00:37:17.453
Take me home.

00:37:25.407 --> 00:37:27.608
Take me home.

00:37:29.440 --> 00:37:30.220
No.

00:38:10.991 --> 00:38:12.240
Don't do this.

00:38:14.822 --> 00:38:16.429
I can never go home.

00:38:19.463 --> 00:38:21.290
You're scared to go home.

00:38:28.290 --> 00:38:29.368
Hold me.

00:38:30.444 --> 00:38:32.896
I'm so cold.

00:38:33.307 --> 00:38:37.288
You can't kill me. I'm not unfaithful.

00:38:37.522 --> 00:38:39.318
I've never been.

00:38:40.530 --> 00:38:41.592
You will be.

00:39:26.118 --> 00:39:27.461
I'm taking you home.

00:39:29.927 --> 00:39:30.489
Sam!

00:39:41.553 --> 00:39:43.317
Sam! Here!

00:39:43.364 --> 00:39:44.504
You okay?

00:39:45.191 --> 00:39:46.065
I think.

00:39:46.659 --> 00:39:48.782
Can you move? Yeah. Help me.

00:40:50.039 --> 00:40:52.208
You've come home to us, mommy.

00:41:30.241 --> 00:41:32.208
So this is where she drowned her kids.

00:41:33.879 --> 00:41:35.347
That's why she could never go home.

00:41:37.134 --> 00:41:38.883
She was too scared to face them.

00:41:40.140 --> 00:41:41.717
You found her weak spot.

00:41:42.185 --> 00:41:43.466
Nice work, Sammy.

00:41:46.046 --> 00:41:48.186
I wish I could say the same for you.

00:41:48.311 --> 00:41:50.599
What were you thinking shooting
Casper in the face, you freak?

00:41:50.704 --> 00:41:53.203
Hey, saved your ass.

00:41:54.092 --> 00:41:57.106
I'll tell you another thing.
If you screwed up my car,

00:41:58.666 --> 00:41:59.884
I'll kill you.

00:42:12.432 --> 00:42:15.663
Okay, here's where dad went. It's
called Blackbottle Ridge, Colorado.

00:42:16.897 --> 00:42:18.661
Sounds charming. How far?

00:42:18.875 --> 00:42:20.732
About 600 miles.

00:42:21.434 --> 00:42:23.761
If we shag ass, we
can make it by morning.

00:42:25.646 --> 00:42:27.207
Dean, um...

00:42:29.784 --> 00:42:30.814
You're not going.

00:42:30.954 --> 00:42:33.375
The interview's in 10
hours. I got to be there.

00:42:38.181 --> 00:42:42.288
Yeah. Yeah, whatever.
I'll take you home.

00:43:02.840 --> 00:43:04.324
You'll call me if you find him?

00:43:07.326 --> 00:43:09.059
Maybe I can meet up with you later, huh?

00:43:09.355 --> 00:43:10.214
Yeah, all right.

00:43:14.208 --> 00:43:14.988
Sam.

00:43:19.048 --> 00:43:20.797
You know, we made a hell
of a team back there.

00:43:22.036 --> 00:43:22.629
Yeah.

00:43:41.845 --> 00:43:42.720
Jess!

00:43:44.594 --> 00:43:45.718
You home!?

00:44:27.772 --> 00:44:28.709
No!

00:44:31.650 --> 00:44:32.618
Sam!

00:44:32.649 --> 00:44:33.414
Jess!

00:44:35.162 --> 00:44:36.677
Sam! Sam!

00:44:37.926 --> 00:44:39.721
No! No!

00:44:40.637 --> 00:44:43.385
Jess! Jess! No!

00:45:29.294 --> 00:45:31.012
We got work to do.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.200
